sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/murrays-law-vascular-optimality> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Does real vasculature obey Murray's law?" ;
    dct:description "At vascular branch points, does the cube of the parent radius equal the sum of the cubes of the daughter radii (Murray's minimum-work law), does the exponent shift toward 2 in high-shear or turbulent beds, and does plant xylem obey the same law?" ;

    skos:historyNote "Known state: Murray (1926) derived the cubic law from minimizing pumping work plus blood-volume maintenance; Sherman (1981) found good agreement in arterial trees; McCulloh, Sperry and Adler (2003) found plant xylem conduits obey Murray's law where conduits are not load-bearing. Modern retinal and whole-organ imaging datasets allow exponent estimation at thousands of branch points, but no standardized cross-tissue, cross-kingdom test exists. Thompson's claim (ch15-13) is the minimum-effort statement." ;
    dct:subject "both" ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "open-problem/tier-B" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Resolved when: A pre-registered test estimating the branching exponent across at least three open vascular datasets (retinal fundus segmentations, micro-CT of organ vasculature, xylem anatomy), with the hypotheses 'exponent 3', 'exponent 7/3 (turbulent)' and 'no single exponent' stated in advance." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Refuted if: Exponent intervals excluding 3 across tissues would refute the general law; a shear-dependent shift would support the amended form." ;
    skos:note "Data access: Open retinal vessel datasets (DRIVE, HRF), open micro-CT vascular casts, xylem data from McCulloh et al. 2003." ;
    skos:note "Requires: image-segmentation" ;
    skos:note "Requires: vascular-morphometry" ;
    skos:note "Requires: data-test" ;
    skos:note "Scale: tissue" ;
    skos:note "Scale: organ" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-13> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-03> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1085/jgp.78.4.431> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01444> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/problems.json> .

  <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207> dct:title "The Physiological Principle of Minimum Work" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Murray 1926, The physiological principle of minimum work I" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1085/jgp.78.4.431> dct:title "On connecting large vessels to small. The meaning of Murray's law." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Sherman 1981, On connecting large vessels to small: the meaning of Murray's law" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01444> dct:title "Water transport in plants obeys Murray's law" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "McCulloh, Sperry and Adler 2003, Water transport in plants obeys Murray's law" .
}

